# Copy to `.env` and edit. Nothing here is secret: every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is
# inlined into the JavaScript the browser downloads, so a key must never be one.
#
# The app runs with this file's defaults and no backend at all. Sign in with
# phone 0914378064, code 111002.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which implementation answers `api.*`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `mock` (the default) fakes every group in the browser; `live` makes real HTTP
# requests to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=mock

# Groups forced live while the rest stay mocked, comma separated. The accepted
# names are `API_GROUPS` in src/api/contracts.ts — `auth` today; the remaining
# groups of docs/api-contract.md (tenant, assistant, receptionist, voice, leads)
# are declared there as the screens that call them arrive.
#
# This exists because Fonnus-BE ships endpoints one at a time over weeks. With
# only a global switch, the first real endpoint could not be exercised until
# every other one existed — which is the difference between integrating
# incrementally and integrating in one terrifying step.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_LIVE_GROUPS=

# Where live requests go. Relative by default so the browser talks to this
# origin and the cookie stays first-party; see docs/adr/0003 for the production
# posture and docs/api-contract.md §1 for why it matters.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development proxy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# In `next dev`, requests to /api/v1/* are rewritten to this origin
# (next.config.ts). Unset means no rewrite — every live call then 404s against
# this app itself, which is the honest failure when the backend is not running.
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shaping the mocks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How long the mock pretends the network takes, in milliseconds. Set to 0 for a
# snappy demo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_LATENCY_MS=450

# Fraction of mock requests that fail, 0..1. Not decoration: the loading,
# rollback and retry paths cannot be reached in mock mode any other way, so this
# is the only way to look at them before a backend exists. Set it to 1 and walk
# the app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_FAILURE_RATE=0
